      "problem": "Which of the following is a zero of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254348/assets/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nThe zeros of the function occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…$\n\nOf the given values, the only one that is a zero of the function is $x=-\\pi .$",
